<div class="page-width">
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h1 class="h1">{{ page_title | default: 'Shop by part type' }}</h1>
      <p class="lede">Every part on this site was pulled from a vehicle on our own lot in Amite. Browse by what the part is, or scroll down and browse by what it came off.</p>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%}
      Two audiences, two groups. Someone who knows they need an alternator wants the part
      type; someone with a dead Ranger in the driveway wants the vehicle. Listing all of
      them flat put ten categories in a wall of a hundred and did neither any favours.

      Categories come from the category-handles snippet, shared with the product
      breadcrumb. Everything else that is not an internal collection is a vehicle.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- capture category_handles -%}{%- render 'category-handles' -%}{%- endcapture -%}
    {%- assign categories = category_handles | strip | split: ',' -%}
    {%- assign internal = 'home-page-picks,just-pulled' | split: ',' -%}

    <div class="grid grid--{{ section.settings.columns }}">
      {%- for collection in collections -%}
        {%- unless categories contains collection.handle -%}{%- continue -%}{%- endunless -%}
        <a href="{{ collection.url }}" class="cat-card">
          {%- if collection.featured_image -%}
            {{ collection.featured_image | image_url: width: 700 | image_tag:
                 widths: '300,500,700', sizes: '(min-width:990px) 320px, 45vw',
                 loading: 'lazy', alt: collection.title }}
          {%- endif -%}
          <span class="cat-card__label">
            {{ collection.title }}
            <small>{{ collection.products_count }} part{% if collection.products_count != 1 %}s{% endif %}</small>
          </span>
        </a>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Vehicles render as links, not cards. They carry no artwork, so a hundred image-less
    cards would be a hundred empty boxes — and a shopper scanning for their own truck
    reads a list far faster than a grid.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign vehicle_count = 0 -%}
  {%- for collection in collections -%}
    {%- unless categories contains collection.handle or internal contains collection.handle -%}
      {%- assign vehicle_count = vehicle_count | plus: 1 -%}
    {%- endunless -%}
  {%- endfor -%}

  {%- if vehicle_count > 0 -%}
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2 class="h2">Shop by vehicle</h2>
      <p class="lede">Every make and model we currently have parts for on the lot. Not seeing yours? Call 985-748-7195 — plenty of the yard is not listed online yet.</p>
    </div>

    <ul class="veh-index">
      {%- for collection in collections -%}
        {%- unless categories contains collection.handle or internal contains collection.handle -%}
          <li>
            <a href="{{ collection.url }}">{{ collection.title | remove: 'Used ' | remove: ' Parts' }}</a>
            <small>{{ collection.products_count }}</small>
          </li>
        {%- endunless -%}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>
  </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Collections list",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "range", "id": "columns", "label": "Columns", "min": 2, "max": 5, "step": 1, "default": 4 }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
